				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-590616#post-3746557</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-590616/i-can-t#post-3746557</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 22 Mar 2018 14:05:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Effervescence</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3420476</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Am I necroing a thread? I just wanted to contribute with my version. Maybe it ruins the poem, but I wanted to 'improve' (opinion) it. Here goes nothing:</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;+</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close&nbsp;-</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>I can't feel your hair anymore,<br /> The river that once streamed down<br /> Out of your head and into my open lap.<br /> It was once silk, always soft to the touch,<br /> But now so sparse, noticeably unfastidious.<br /> So frayed, wired in a chaotic disarray.</p> <p>I can't feel your face anymore,<br /> The mask kept immaculate upon your head.<br /> Impeccable as it was,<br /> No matter how absolute it looked<br /> Became so broken.<br /> Now cracked with crevices.</p> <p>I can't feel your hand anymore, a thing that was so fragile<br /> Threatening to crumble even if you just looked at it.<br /> It was once dainty, so delicate,<br /> But now so bent and callused.<br /> Now singed and pulverized.</p> <p>I can't feel your touch, something I've loved<br /> Ever since we had once met long ago.<br /> It once was stimulating, exhilarating,<br /> But now gone and so far away.<br /> How far could it possibly be?</p> <p>I can't feel your pulse anymore,<br /> the rhythmic drumming when I first left my hands to caress your chess,<br /> I can't feel it against my bloodstained hands anymore.<br /> I can't feel it.<br /> I can't.</p> </div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
